      "side": 1,
      "message": "The `_POSIX_C_SOURCE` macro is not Linux-specific. I suggest defining it here, next to the two related macro definitions:\n\n```\n  add_compiler_flag_if_supported(\"-D_POSIX_C_SOURCE\u003d200112L\")\n```\n\nIf it is necessary to define `_POSIX_C_SOURCE` at the location you proposed, we should move these two related macto definitions there, and change the condition to `if (NOT WIN32)`.\n\n---\n\nNote: My colleague Vincent Rebaud and I dealt with this issue in libavif before. Here is our solution in [libavif/src/io.c](https://github.com/AOMediaCodec/libavif/blob/main/src/io.c):\n\n```\n#if !defined(_WIN32)\n// Ensure off_t is 64 bits.\n#undef _FILE_OFFSET_BITS\n#define _FILE_OFFSET_BITS 64\n// Ensure we have some POSIX compatibility with fseeko/ftello.\n#undef _POSIX_C_SOURCE\n#define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L\n#endif\n```\n\nSo the only essential difference is the condition (MSVC vs. WIN32).",
      "revId": "b78622d62486ecbb59a73a24e3c2d7d669af7374",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    }
